## Description

The DFlash 2 candidate selector scores position `t` under the candidate at `t - 1`, and it is trained with the true previous token there. With `use_rejection_sampling`, `DFlashWorker` approximated this:
- it scored every position under the greedy walk's argmax predecessors;
- then it sampled each position independently.

The approximation is lossless. But once a draw leaves the argmax, later positions are scored under a token the block does not contain. That costs acceptance from position 2 on: acceptance length is 8% lower at draft length 7 than in SGLan

## Purpose

This PR brings the CPU top-k/top-p sampling work from #43452 and #55874 to the current vLLM main branch while preserving the original commit authorship:

- Tianmu Li's commit adds the base C++ kernels and integration for top-k, top-p, and combined top-k/top-p sampling.
- Fadi Arafeh's commit adds the AArch64 implementation.

The final cleanup commit:

- removes the AVX512 and AVX2 sampling paths introduced by the base implementation;
- retains the AArch64 implementation and scalar fallbacks;
- removes the added AVX2 fast-exp macro and `-mfma` build flag;
- applies repository format

